1
00:00:04,970 --> 00:00:08,210
弗里曼：永恒。
Freeman: Eternity.

2
00:00:08,230 --> 00:00:11,240
是个宗教般古老的概念。
It's an idea as old as religion.

3
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:16,230
或是伴随着人类的诞生而出现。
Perhaps as old as humankind.

4
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:21,630
但是现代科学能告诉我们时间尽头是什么吗？
But what can modern science tell us about the end of time?

5
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:28,770
这一切会在宇宙末日时结束吗？
Will the Universe end in a cosmic apocalypse?

6
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:32,440
时间会永远“滴答”下去...
Could time keep on ticking forever...

7
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:38,480
还是最终会走向结束？
Or will eternity end?

8
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:48,190
《同摩根·弗里曼一起穿越虫洞》
空间、时间、生命本身
Space, time, life itself.

9
00:00:50,490 --> 00:00:54,860
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

10
00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:03,890
永恒会终结吗？

11
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:09,750
世界末日
The Apocalypse.

12
00:01:09,750 --> 00:01:13,980
是穆斯林、基督徒和犹太人相信的
It's the day when Muslims, Christians, and Jews

13
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:18,590
我们周围的世界崩坏的那一天。
believe the world will come crashing down around us.

14
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:22,430
现在，物理学家有他们自己对于末日的看法。
Physicists now have their own version of Apocalypse.

15
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:25,900
事实上，世界末日有这么几个版本，
In fact, they have several of them.

16
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:28,630
太阳吞没了地球、
The sun will engulf the earth.

17
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:32,270
我们坠入了黑洞、
Our star will fall into a black hole.

18
00:01:32,270 --> 00:01:36,970
我们的银河系与另一星系发生碰撞...
Our entire galaxy will collide with another.

19
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:40,740
那如果万物都终结呢？
But what if everything came to an end?

20
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:44,550
一切尽毁于这场灾难
Destroyed in an Apocalypse so complete

21
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:47,920
以至于时间也不复存在。
that time itself would disappear.

22
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:58,330
在我还是孩子的时候，我奶奶去世了。
I was just a young boy when time ran out for my grandmother.

23
00:02:01,870 --> 00:02:05,640
太阳每日仍东升西落，
The sun continued to rise and set each day.

24
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:07,600
四季周而复始。
The seasons cycled on.

25
00:02:07,610 --> 00:02:12,240
我想为什么属于我奶奶的时间结束了，
I wondered if time for my grandmother really had ended,

26
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:15,680
而宇宙的时间仍在继续。
time when the Universe carried on.

27
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:21,320
实际上，时间本身会结束看起来不太可能。
In fact, it seemed impossible that time itself could ever end.

28
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:27,860
古希腊和古埃及人
The ancient Greeks and Egyptians

29
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:31,260
将永恒置于时间之外。
thought of eternity as a place outside of time.

30
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:33,500
他们认为时间是一个循环，
They saw time as a giant circle,

31
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:36,570
就像太阳每日经过我们的头顶
mirroring the passing of the sun overhead

32
00:02:36,570 --> 00:02:38,800
就像春夏秋冬的循环。
and the rotation of the seasons.

33
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:45,940
到了今日，我们已经把时间铺成了一条线
But today, we have rolled out the circle of time into a line

34
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:49,710
从久远的过去，延伸到遥远的未来。
stretching from the distant past to the far future.

35
00:02:49,710 --> 00:02:55,050
现在我们必须思考这条时间线是否会有终点
Now we are forced to contemplate whether this timeline has an end

36
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:58,390
还是会无尽的延伸下去。
or whether it can stretch on forever.

37
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,960
但是，永恒这一谜题
But perhaps the riddle of eternity

38
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:05,660
或许仅是我们大脑中创造出来的。
is something we've created in our heads.

39
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:11,470
人类学家Vera da Silva Sinha
Anthropologist Vera da Silva Sinha

40
00:03:11,470 --> 00:03:15,040
和语言心理学家Chris Sinha
and linguistic psychologist Chris Sinha

41
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:20,140
一直费尽心思来看人们是如何看待时间的。
spend their time thinking about how people think about time.

42
00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:24,210
Chris：我们拥有一个很大尺度上的复杂社会。
Chris: We have very large-scale, complex societies.

43
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:27,450
我们无法传承我们的社会
We could not make our society take over

44
00:03:27,450 --> 00:03:30,820
如果我们没有个日历或一块表。
if we didn't have a calendar and a clock.

45
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:35,360
所以我们认为时间这一概念和测量时间的方法
So we think of time concepts and ways of measuring time

46
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:39,260
成为了一种我们称之为的“认知技术”。
as being what we call a "cognitive technology."

47
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,700
这是一种思维的技术。
It's a technology of the mind.

48
00:03:41,700 --> 00:03:45,800
弗里曼：但是Chris和Vera发现
Freeman: But Chris and Vera have discovered

49
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:49,310
这种对时间有组织的看法并不普遍。
this organized view of time is not universal.

50
00:03:49,310 --> 00:03:51,370
他们得到这种结论源于
It's an insight they gained

51
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:54,410
对亚马逊河流域的一个被称作Amondawa
(阿莫达瓦)的当地土著的
from studying the language and culture

52
00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:58,550
语言和文化的学习。
of an indigenous Amazonian tribe called the Amondawa.

53
00:03:58,550 --> 00:04:01,950
阿莫达瓦人居住在Rondonia--
The Amondawa people live in Rondonia --

54
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:03,190
巴西的一个州。
the state of Brazil.

55
00:04:03,190 --> 00:04:05,820
巴西政府于1984年与此部落
They were contacted by the Brazilian government

56
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:08,460
建立了联系。
in 1984.

57
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:12,200
阿莫达瓦部落并不依赖日历生活，
The Amondawa tribe does not live by a calendar,

58
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:14,230
而且他们也不用表。
and they don't use clocks.

59
00:04:14,230 --> 00:04:18,830
实际上，他们的语言中甚至没有像时间这样的词汇
In fact, there isn't even a word for time in their language.

60
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:22,370
如果你去问一个阿莫达瓦人
If you ask an Amondawa speaker

61
00:04:22,370 --> 00:04:24,940
让他翻译“时间”这个词，
to give a translation of the word "time,"

62
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:27,640
他们能够想到的最近义的词是--
the nearest thing that they can think of --

63
00:04:27,650 --> 00:04:29,450
“太阳”，
they will say "Sun."

64
00:04:29,450 --> 00:04:32,220
或是“雨季”。
Or they say "raining season,"

65
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:35,790
又或是“夏日”，但就是没有...
or they say "summertime," but there is no...

66
00:04:35,790 --> 00:04:38,750
没有一个关于时间的词，对吧？
There's nothing which is abstracted from that, right?

67
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:43,060
为了试图理解阿莫达瓦人对于时间的概念，
To try and understand the Amondawa's notion of time,

68
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:47,700
Chris和Vera在他们面前放了一系列纸盘子。
Chris and Vera had them arrange a series of paper plates.

69
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:51,570
那么，我们发现这只有两个季节，对吗？
So, we found out there is two seasons, yeah?

70
00:04:51,570 --> 00:04:54,400
雨季和旱季。
Rain season and dry season.

71
00:04:54,410 --> 00:04:58,110
然后，他们要用这些盘子
So, and they would use the plates

72
00:04:58,110 --> 00:05:02,040
来表示如何将这些季节区分。
to symbolize how these seasons are divided.

73
00:05:02,050 --> 00:05:05,250
一名阿莫达瓦人会将这些盘子排列起来
An Amondawa man organizes the plates

74
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:09,950
并不是根据天或月，而是根据发生在
not according to days or months but by the natural events

75
00:05:09,950 --> 00:05:13,360
这两个季节中的自然事件。
that occur throughout their two seasons.

76
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:17,690
对于每个季节的细分来说，
For each one of these small subdivisions of a season,

77
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:21,100
他会告诉你个小故事
he'll tell a little story

78
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:24,830
都是一些关于种植或收获什么，
about what kind of planting and harvesting goes on,

79
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:27,240
什么水果成熟了，
also what fruits are ripening

80
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:31,040
还有在森林和河流中发生了什么，
and what's going on in the forest and in the rivers.

81
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:33,680
河流水位上升还是下降？
Is their level of the river going up or going down?

82
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:34,740
就是这一类的事。
This kind of thing.

83
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:35,980
是的，是的。
Yeah. Yeah.

84
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:38,310
这是一种对于时间的描绘
It's a way of mapping out time

85
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:41,320
对于每个农民都有意义。
that would make sense to any farmer.

86
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:44,220
但是在我们的工业文明中，
But in our industrialized cultures,

87
00:05:44,220 --> 00:05:47,490
取而代之的是个更为严格的系统。
a much more rigid system has taken over.

88
00:05:47,490 --> 00:05:50,130
我们可能把这些盘子并排放7个--
We might arrange plates in a line of seven --

89
00:05:50,130 --> 00:05:53,060
每个盘子代表了一周的一天。
one plate for each day of the week.

90
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:58,230
或是我们把一天按照小时数放成一圈。
Or we would divide a day into hours arranged in a circle.

91
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:02,540
但阿莫达瓦人不会以其他的形式排列事件。
But the Amondawa don't arrange events in any particular shape.

92
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:08,540
Vera：他不会关心这些事件的形式。
Vera: He's not really worried about the shape of the events.

93
00:06:08,550 --> 00:06:11,610
他关心的是每个事件的内容。
He worry about the contents of each event.

94
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:14,680
他们不认为时间是类似于
They don't think of time as being analogous

95
00:06:14,690 --> 00:06:16,590
空间中的一个维度。
to a spacial dimension.

96
00:06:16,590 --> 00:06:19,490
他们不认为时间是条线，
They don't think of time being a sort of line

97
00:06:19,490 --> 00:06:23,030
顺着它向前看是未来，
in which there is a future that you look forward to

98
00:06:23,030 --> 00:06:25,490
向后则是过去。
and a past that you look back to.

99
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:28,730
你可以用英语说“哦，我想起了我的小时候。”
In English, you can say, "Oh, I look back to my childhood."

100
00:06:28,730 --> 00:06:31,800
而对于阿莫达瓦人，你并不能回顾你的孩童时期。
However, in Amondawa, you don't look back to your childhood.

101
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,900
所以，你还是孩子的时候，你就是在那个时候。
So, in your childhood, you were there,

102
00:06:33,910 --> 00:06:35,670
所以你不会再往回看。
so you don't look back anymore.

103
00:06:35,670 --> 00:06:37,940
所以[笑]
So [Chuckles]

104
00:06:37,940 --> 00:06:40,840
阿莫达瓦人不会顺着时间线
The Amondawa don't look back on a line

105
00:06:40,850 --> 00:06:44,110
从过去到现在回顾自己的生活。
that traces their life from past to present.

106
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:45,980
但在西方文明，
But in Western cultures,

107
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:50,050
我们不禁将这个时间几何加入我们的生活。
we can't help but impose this time geometry on our lives.

108
00:06:50,050 --> 00:06:52,390
一个人的一生就像一条线
A person's life is like a line

109
00:06:52,390 --> 00:06:54,790
从出生延伸到死亡，
that stretches from birth to death,

110
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:57,790
我们同时会想象宇宙也是这样，
and so we imagine the Universe, too,

111
00:06:57,800 --> 00:07:00,160
肯定会有一条时间线--
must have a timeline --

112
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:04,430
从140亿年前的大爆炸出生
from its birth in the Big Bang, 14 billion years ago

113
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:08,200
到它遥远未来时的死亡。
to some far future date when it will die.

114
00:07:10,410 --> 00:07:13,580
在宇宙诞生前并没有时间，
There was no time before the beginning,

115
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:16,380
而在宇宙最终毁灭的时候，
and time will eventually disappear

116
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:19,880
时间也随之消失。
when the Universe meets its apocalyptic end.

117
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:25,550
理论物理学家Fotini Markopoulou,
Theoretical physicist Fotini Markopoulou,

118
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:29,490
就像阿莫达瓦人，否认这一观点。
like the Amondawa, rejects this idea.

119
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:32,600
好吧，如果你要说时间会终结，
Well, if you are to say that time will end,

120
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:35,160
那你必须要说时间出现的时候。
you also have to say that time began.

121
00:07:35,170 --> 00:07:36,870
就像死亡和出生。
It's like death and birth.

122
00:07:36,870 --> 00:07:39,770
不可能只有死亡而没有出生。
You really can't have deaths and no births.

123
00:07:39,770 --> 00:07:42,000
那么现在你要告诉我
So now you have to tell me

124
00:07:42,010 --> 00:07:45,640
如果没有时间，时间从哪儿来？
where time came from if there was no time.

125
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:49,010
弗里曼：Fotini一直试图理解
Freeman: Fotini is trying to understand

126
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:51,550
时间的基本性质，
the fundamental nature of time,

127
00:07:51,550 --> 00:07:55,920
这对于微观世界的亚原子粒子
which in the microscopic world of subatomic particles

128
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:58,020
是一个微妙的概念。
becomes a tricky concept.

129
00:07:58,020 --> 00:08:00,720
量子力学理论认为
The theory of Quantum Mechanics says

130
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:02,760
粒子不会是以颗粒、确定的物体
that particles don't interact

131
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:05,590
相互作用，
as if they are solid, defined objects,

132
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:07,330
而以无实体云这种形式。
but as amorphous clouds.

133
00:08:07,330 --> 00:08:10,230
一个粒子可以在那里
A particle can be both there

134
00:08:10,230 --> 00:08:13,840
而又同时不在那里。
and not there at the same time.

135
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:17,440
这样就不可能知道两个粒子什么时候相遇
And it's impossible to say when two particles meet

136
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:19,980
或是它们是否会相遇。
or whether they did at all.

137
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:23,810
如果你要把量子力学的定律
If you try to apply the laws of Quantum Mechanics

138
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:27,080
应用到宏观物体上，比如人类或星球，
to large objects like people or planets,

139
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:31,690
你能想象到一些非常让人迷惑的可能。
you can imagine some very puzzling possibilities.

140
00:08:31,690 --> 00:08:33,720
我坐在这儿，我正跟你说话。
I'm sitting here, and I'm talking to you.

141
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:37,790
现在，如果我们的宇宙中，
Now, if by some accident, in our Universe,

142
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:39,560
有一个巨型黑洞
there was a huge black hole

143
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:42,330
会把我吸进黑洞中，
that would suck me inside the black hole,

144
00:08:42,330 --> 00:08:43,800
根据量子理论，
according to Quantum Theory,

145
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:47,340
我身后的这个黑洞可能会存在，同时也不存在。
that black hole behind me should be there and not there.

146
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:50,810
这样，结果呢，你所参与的我们的这次交谈
And, as a result, you are in a position of our conversation

147
00:08:50,810 --> 00:08:53,010
发生了或是没有发生。
having happened or not happened.

148
00:08:54,380 --> 00:08:56,880
弗里曼：许多量子物理学家认为
Freeman: Many Quantum physicists argue

149
00:08:56,880 --> 00:09:00,780
这种事件是否发生的不确定性
this uncertainty over whether the events really happened

150
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:03,850
表明了时间并不是我们宇宙的一个
shows that time cannot be a fundamental thing

151
00:09:03,860 --> 00:09:05,050
基本性质。
in the Universe.

152
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:06,990
而是一些我们自己捏造出来的。
It's something we've made up.

153
00:09:06,990 --> 00:09:10,960
阿尔伯特爱因斯坦并不赞同量子力学。
Albert Einstein disagreed with Quantum Mechanics.

154
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:13,000
他认为时间是真实存在的，
He believed time is real,

155
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:17,700
它和空间交织在宇宙的纤维中。
that it is woven with space into the fabric of the Universe.

156
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:20,240
根据他学生的观点，
And, according to his disciples,

157
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:24,040
空间和时间同时产生于大爆炸。
space and time were born together in the Big Bang.

158
00:09:25,310 --> 00:09:29,980
但是Fotini认为这些对于时间的观点都有问题。
But Fotini thinks both these views of time are wrong.

159
00:09:29,980 --> 00:09:33,750
她认为时间是真的，而且是永恒的。
She thinks that time is real and eternal.

160
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:35,820
但如果这是真相，
But for that to be true,

161
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:38,920
我们就要重新想象空间是什么。
we have to reimagine what space is.

162
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:41,420
好吧，比如这就是--
Okay, so let's say that this is space --

163
00:09:41,430 --> 00:09:42,860
我们生活的空间--
the world we live in --

164
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:48,430
这些红绳是我们世界中的一些东西。
and the little red strings are other stuff in our world.

165
00:09:48,430 --> 00:09:51,570
网表示我们之间的距离
And the net represents the distances between us

166
00:09:51,570 --> 00:09:53,270
就网格连接而言。
in terms of connectivity.

167
00:09:53,270 --> 00:09:55,600
这就是说，例如，
So that means that, for instance,

168
00:09:55,610 --> 00:09:57,310
如果我说这是我
if we say that this is me

