00:37:34,780 --> 00:37:38,050
这个空间-时间区域，
That region in space-time,

680
00:37:38,050 --> 00:37:39,480
形成了一个菱形，
it forms a diamond shape

681
00:37:39,490 --> 00:37:42,420
因为光像这样的一个锥形辐射出来，
because light goes out in sort of a cone like this,

682
00:37:42,420 --> 00:37:45,060
接着我从最近的时刻往回看，
and then if I look back from the latest time,

683
00:37:45,060 --> 00:37:46,660
形成一个反向的锥形，
it goes backwards in a cone.

684
00:37:46,660 --> 00:37:48,730
把这两个锥形放一起，
You put those two cones together,

685
00:37:48,730 --> 00:37:50,930
它们就构成了菱形。
and they're sort of a diamond shape.

686
00:37:50,930 --> 00:37:53,500
[钟表滴答声]
[ Clock ticking ]

687
00:37:53,500 --> 00:37:56,200
弗里曼：一个因果菱形标志着
Freeman: A causal diamond marks the limit

688
00:37:56,200 --> 00:37:59,170
一个测量设备能够测量到的
of how much of the Universe a measuring device

689
00:37:59,170 --> 00:38:00,810
宇宙的极限。
could ever hope to reach.

690
00:38:00,810 --> 00:38:03,910
当这个设备发射出一道光线，
When that device sends out a light beam,

691
00:38:03,910 --> 00:38:06,180
它指向广袤的宇宙中，
it heads out into the Universe,

692
00:38:06,180 --> 00:38:08,910
并被遥远的星系反射回来，
bounces off some distant galaxies,

693
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:13,150
亿万年之后光线被这个设备接收到。
and finally returns to the device billions of years later.

694
00:38:13,150 --> 00:38:15,390
Tom能够计算出
Tom has been able to calculate

695
00:38:15,390 --> 00:38:19,690
菱形内部存在的信息量，
that the amount of information existing inside that diamond

696
00:38:19,690 --> 00:38:22,060
这些信息形成一个球体区域，
is related to the area of a sphere

697
00:38:22,060 --> 00:38:26,560
直径恰好相当于菱形的长对角线，
that just fits around it at its widest point,

698
00:38:26,570 --> 00:38:30,270
Tom称之为“全息屏幕”。
a sphere he calls "the holographic screen."

699
00:38:30,270 --> 00:38:32,470
Banks：现在我们可以问个问题，
Banks: So now we can ask the question,

700
00:38:32,470 --> 00:38:35,140
假设有可以从宇宙的开始
suppose there was some machine that lived forever

701
00:38:35,140 --> 00:38:37,710
运行到宇宙终结的机器，
from the beginning of the Universe to the end?

702
00:38:37,710 --> 00:38:41,080
那么这个无限存在的探测器
How big does the holographic screen of the causal diamond

703
00:38:41,080 --> 00:38:43,980
所得到的的因果菱形的全息屏幕有多大呢？
of that infinitely long-lived detector ever get?

704
00:38:43,980 --> 00:38:45,450
这点很重要，
And it's very important,

705
00:38:45,450 --> 00:38:48,150
因为这决定了
because that determines how much information

706
00:38:48,150 --> 00:38:49,850
这个空间和时间的区域中
there could've possibly been

707
00:38:49,860 --> 00:38:51,990
会有多少信息。
in this region of space and time.

708
00:38:51,990 --> 00:38:56,290
弗里曼：知道一切意味着
Freeman: Knowing absolutely everything there is to know

709
00:38:56,300 --> 00:39:00,800
要知道每个原子和亚原子粒子的存在，
about every atom and every subatomic particle in existence

710
00:39:00,800 --> 00:39:05,270
这就是说要搜集让人兴奋的信息量。
would mean collecting a truly mind-blowing amount of data.

711
00:39:05,270 --> 00:39:09,440
Banks：这个数是10的10次方的123次方，
Banks: This number is 10 to the 10 to the 123.

712
00:39:09,440 --> 00:39:13,280
就是1后面有10的123次方个0。
It's a 1 with 10 to the 123 zeros after it.

713
00:39:13,280 --> 00:39:17,620
这个数太大了，让人很难想象。
That number is so huge that it's hard to imagine it.

714
00:39:17,620 --> 00:39:21,450
如果我把这个数写下来
If I started trying to write that number down

715
00:39:21,450 --> 00:39:24,090
每秒钟写一个零，
and I wrote a zero every second,

716
00:39:24,090 --> 00:39:26,090
我需要的时间
I would run out of time

717
00:39:26,090 --> 00:39:29,990
比整个宇宙的历史还要长，
long before the whole history of the Universe,

718
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:32,500
恐怕我永远都无法把这个数写完。
and I would never get to the end of it.

719
00:39:32,500 --> 00:39:35,800
弗里曼：但是一个先进的文明
Freeman: But could an advanced civilization

720
00:39:35,800 --> 00:39:38,040
到底能不能搜集这么多数据
actually collect this much data

721
00:39:38,040 --> 00:39:40,940
来了解宇宙中的一切，
and know everything about the Universe

722
00:39:40,940 --> 00:39:42,740
然后了解它的命运？
and thus learn its fate?

723
00:39:42,740 --> 00:39:44,680
Tom认为，
The answer, Tom believes,

724
00:39:44,680 --> 00:39:49,580
答案就包含在这一小杯水中。
is contained in this tiny cup of water.

725
00:39:49,580 --> 00:39:53,520
这一点水是我刚从太平洋中取出的，
So, in this little bit of water I just got out of the Pacific,

726
00:39:53,520 --> 00:39:55,290
这有10的21次方个原子。
there are sextillion atoms.

727
00:39:55,290 --> 00:39:57,220
相当于数万亿的数万亿个。
That's trillions of trillions.

728
00:39:57,220 --> 00:39:59,820
如果我们想测量所有的这些原子，
If we wanted to measure all those atoms,

729
00:39:59,830 --> 00:40:02,360
我们必须有一个相当大的仪器，
we'd have to have a really big machine.

730
00:40:02,360 --> 00:40:06,430
这个设备可能比美国还大。
We'd need a device that was larger than the United States.

731
00:40:06,430 --> 00:40:10,270
弗里曼：但是搜集宇宙中所有的信息
Freeman: But collecting data on the entire Universe

732
00:40:10,270 --> 00:40:13,270
不仅仅是一项不朽的工程挑战，
is not just a monumental engineering challenge.

733
00:40:13,270 --> 00:40:17,710
物理学法则也在阻止我们这么做。
The laws of physics actually prevent us from doing it.

734
00:40:17,710 --> 00:40:20,980
如果我们要测量存在的每个原子，
If we tried to measure every atom in existence,

735
00:40:20,980 --> 00:40:23,780
我们最终会因为使用如此巨大的设备
we would end up using so much equipment

736
00:40:23,780 --> 00:40:27,720
巨大到我们无法操作，
that we'd fill space with more stuff than it could handle,

737
00:40:27,720 --> 00:40:31,690
整个实验就会坍缩成一个黑洞，
and the entire experiment would collapse into a black hole,

738
00:40:31,690 --> 00:40:34,560
又把所有的信息给毁了。
destroying all that information with it.

739
00:40:34,560 --> 00:40:36,230
哇哦！
Whoa!

740
00:40:38,260 --> 00:40:41,830
Tom计算出来，我们只能
Tom has calculated that we can measure no more

741
00:40:41,830 --> 00:40:45,440
测量少于10的10的90次方字节的信息，
than 10 to the 10 to the 90 bits of information

742
00:40:45,440 --> 00:40:49,040
才能不会造成整个宇宙
before we cause the entire Universe to collapse

743
00:40:49,040 --> 00:40:50,540
坍缩成黑洞。
into a black hole.

744
00:40:50,540 --> 00:40:53,180
这看起来像是一个无比巨大的数字，
This may seem like a gigantic number,

745
00:40:53,180 --> 00:40:55,910
其实这仅仅是一丁点数据，
but it is actually just a tiny fraction

746
00:40:55,920 --> 00:40:58,650
相对于10的10的123次方
of 10 to the 10 to the 123,

747
00:40:58,650 --> 00:41:02,750
（知道一切）来说。
which is all that there is to know.

748
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:06,390
我们能知道的数据远比代表一切的数字少，
That number is so incredibly smaller than this number,

749
00:41:06,390 --> 00:41:09,360
所以一个文明
that there's no hope that any civilization,

750
00:41:09,360 --> 00:41:11,260
无论有多么尖端，
no matter how sophisticated,

751
00:41:11,260 --> 00:41:14,370
也没有希望能够测量
could possibly measure all of the information

752
00:41:14,370 --> 00:41:18,340
整个宇宙历史的全部信息。
that there is in the Universe throughout its entire history.

753
00:41:18,340 --> 00:41:22,340
弗里曼：我们对宇宙的所有了解
Freeman: All we can ever learn about the Universe

754
00:41:22,340 --> 00:41:26,310
是极度少量。
is an impossibly tiny morsel of what's out there.

755
00:41:26,310 --> 00:41:27,750
Tom认为，
And Tom argues,

756
00:41:27,750 --> 00:41:32,220
试图基于如此少的知识量来预测宇宙的未来
trying to predict the future based on such scant knowledge

757
00:41:32,220 --> 00:41:33,780
是完全没用的。
is utterly futile.

758
00:41:33,790 --> 00:41:39,260
那么或许我们不应该去考虑时间的结束，
So, perhaps we should quit worrying about the end of time

759
00:41:39,260 --> 00:41:42,160
只需要学会生活在当下。（译者极不赞同这种观点）
and learn to live for the now.

760
00:41:42,160 --> 00:41:45,660
Banks：想要了解一切是我们的本性，
Banks: It's natural for us to want to know everything.

761
00:41:45,670 --> 00:41:50,130
我们喜欢用所有的事来编故事，
And we like to make up stories about everything.

762
00:41:50,140 --> 00:41:52,940
但通常那些故事都不是真的，
And those stories are often wrong.

763
00:41:52,940 --> 00:41:55,110
所以人类...才是人类，
So people...are people.

764
00:41:55,110 --> 00:41:58,080
我们是有限的，我们不是神。
We're finite. We're not Gods.

765
00:41:58,080 --> 00:42:00,580
我们--我们不拥有宇宙，
We're -- we don't own the Universe.

766
00:42:00,580 --> 00:42:03,350
我们只是宇宙中的极小的一部分，
We're a very tiny portion of the Universe.

767
00:42:03,350 --> 00:42:07,150
现在我们发现，我们比我们以前想象的
And we've now discovered that we're a much tinier portion

768
00:42:07,150 --> 00:42:09,320
更加微小。
than we might've thought before.

769
00:42:09,320 --> 00:42:12,090
某种意义上来说，我们没有权利
We don't have the right, in some sense,

770
00:42:12,090 --> 00:42:15,560
来期望知道一切。
to expect to know everything that there is to know.

771
00:42:20,030 --> 00:42:23,470
宇宙会永远发展下去吗？
Will the Universe last forever?

772
00:42:23,470 --> 00:42:25,970
永恒早已存在，
Is eternity already out there,

773
00:42:25,970 --> 00:42:30,510
只是把“将来”的我们投影到“现在”吗？
projecting the present back to us from the far future?

774
00:42:30,510 --> 00:42:34,480
还是一场大灾难会在一瞬间
Or will a cosmic apocalypse destroy everything

775
00:42:34,480 --> 00:42:36,480
毁灭一切？
in the blink of an eye?

776
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:40,250
我们还不知道，或许我们永远也不知道，
We don't know, and we probably never will,

777
00:42:40,250 --> 00:42:44,260
因为解答这个问题需要的知识，
because some questions require more knowledge

778
00:42:44,260 --> 00:42:46,190
比我们能得到的更多。
than we can ever get.

779
00:42:46,190 --> 00:42:49,530
也有可能事实并不这么糟糕。
And maybe that's not so bad.

780
00:42:49,530 --> 00:42:53,760
毕竟如果我们知道未来如何结束，
After all, what fun would life be

781
00:42:53,770 --> 00:42:57,400
那生命还有什么乐趣呢？
if we already knew how it was going to end?

